  "ingredients": [
    "2 tablespoons herbes de Provence",
    "1.5 tablespoons olive oil",
    "2 cloves garlic, minced",
    "2 teaspoons lemon juice",
    "8 (5 ounce) lamb loin chops",
    "salt and ground black pepper to taste"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather the ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/HbRKGNwnhr4Kj9Iaa5723xNVIDk=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/274989-grilled-lamb-loin-chops-ddmfs-step1-4451-b223d72f8c2040818fcada22aaf20043.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/274989/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine herbes de Provence, oil, garlic, and lemon juice in a small bowl.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/MNW52c4qaWJycvGzdUO27J6VCMI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/274989-grilled-lamb-loin-chops-ddmfs-step2-4453-98008dcbe0144442b28a2f48251be902.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/274989/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rub mixture over lamb chops; cover and refrigerate for at least 1 hour, or up to 4 hours for maximum flavor.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/nWR7L-QRezkh8MHIDzsOcEUsN5o=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/274989-grilled-lamb-loin-chops-ddmfs-step3-4454-ab7180c7c60b4bae9df5051a08491a60.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/274989/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat and lightly oil the grate.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Season chops with salt and pepper.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/SaEonb7-jg0IlBvllY4DIEYXB6c=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/274989-grilled-lamb-loin-chops-ddmfs-step4-4456-dfb82b4250394151b7f347bbb5a25eb1.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/274989/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place chops on the preheated grill and cook until browned on the outside and an instant-read thermometer inserted into the center reads at least 125 degrees F (52 degrees C) for medium-rare, 3 to 4 minutes per side. Transfer chops to an aluminum foil-covered plate; let rest for 5 minutes before serving.",
